Implement a new TypeScript module with this public API:

```typescript
export interface ActionSpec {
  id: string;
  label: string;
  run: () => void;
}

export interface ActionView {
  id: string;
  label: string;
}

export class ActionPanel {
  constructor(actions: readonly ActionSpec[]);
  items(): ReadonlyArray<ActionView>;
  trigger(id: string): void;
}
```

The constructor must accept an empty array. Every action must have a non-empty, already-trimmed `id`, a non-empty `label`, and a function-valued `run`; malformed entries must cause `TypeError`. IDs must be unique or the constructor must throw `Error`. Preserve input ordering and copy each action so later mutation of the input array or its objects cannot change the panel. `items()` must return a newly allocated, frozen array containing frozen view objects, with no callback exposed. `trigger` must reject a non-string or empty ID with `TypeError`, invoke exactly the callback whose ID exactly matches, and throw `Error` for an unknown ID.

